.TH grmb "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
grmb \- Delete a git branch locally and on origin
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B grmb
.I BRANCH_NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B grmb
(git remove branch) force deletes
.I BRANCH_NAME
locally with
.B git branch -D
and then deletes it on the
.B origin
remote with
.BR "git push origin --delete" .
.PP
The local delete is forced, so a branch is removed even when it is not merged.
There is no confirmation: only run it on a branch that is really finished.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the remote delete.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.B grmb feature/old-experiment
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR smi-new-tag (1)
